{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This trip was sold on an upfront quote, not a meter: fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE and quoted_fare_sgd is 21.50. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront trip, and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however long the route turned out to be. The route-length element of the rider's complaint therefore yields nothing on those lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The measured excess on this trip's own trace is 3.22 km against a booked optimal of 9.2 km, or 35.00%. That clears the establishment gates of POL-RD-01 (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but is below both materiality gates in the same clause (greater than 50% of optimal, or greater than 8.0 km absolute). This is at most an ordinary established deviation: POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not triggered by it, so no FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral can follow from this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02813", "EV-TRIP-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taken at its highest the rider's monetary claim is capped by POL-RD-11(a) at the amount by which charged_total (28.30) exceeds quoted_fare_sgd (21.50) plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable (0.00) - that is 6.80, not the 7.50 the rider contests. To that extent the claim is not made out, and the remedy is arithmetic rather than discretionary: no clause in this policy licenses a goodwill or round-number payment for the route itself.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the fare ledger enlarges that figure. There is no ERP line and no toll (erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00), no airport surcharge (0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport), and the waiting-time fee is nil - so no standalone pass-through or billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09 arises to add to the 6.80 over-quote figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.properly_chargeable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's record gives the tribunal no basis to treat this as a repeat-deviation matter even if POL-RD-06 were consulted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 260, far below either limb of the clause's pattern test (three or more flags, or a ratio of 0.05 or more). No pattern is established against this driver on the only fields POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit for that test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02813"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.8,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This is a provisional automated ruling issued without human review (POL-GEN-08(2)); either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. The rider filed; SGD 7.50 is contested on a fare quoted at SGD 21.50 and charged at SGD 28.30. The outcome is a partial refund of SGD 6.80. WHAT IS AGREED AND FOUND. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02813), the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02813) and the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02813) all carry trip_id TRP-02813 and the trace's first fix (13:59:11) matches the recorded meter start, so the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. The trace carries 98 fixes at 10 s with 100% coverage, no gaps and a 0 s maximum gap, so it is NOT impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) and no independent corroboration is required; the settlement goes forward on the trace. Under the trace-governs rule of POL-RD-01 the governing figure is gps_trace.trace_distance_km 12.42 km, not the rounded 12.4 km copy on the trip record. Against the booked optimal of 9.2 km the excess is 3.22 km / 35.00%, which clears both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) but clears neither materiality gate (greater than 50% or greater than 8.0 km). Both advocates put the deviation at that level and I accept it: a deviation is ESTABLISHED but is NOT MATERIAL. THE MONEY. The trip is priced on an upfront quote (EV-FARE-02813, fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 21.50). Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and POL-RD-02 does not run, so no distance-or-time refund is available however long the route driven was; the driver's claim to that effect is accepted, and the route-length part of the rider's complaint yields nothing on those lines. The rider's remedy is POL-RD-11(a): charged_total 28.30 less quoted_fare_sgd 21.50 less properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines 0.00 = 6.80, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 6.80. Nothing changes that figure: there is no ERP or toll line (tolls_erp 0.00, erp_gantries empty), no airport surcharge (0.00, and none could be properly chargeable on a trip from Jurong Point to a Clementi residential block), and waiting_time_fee 0.00, so POL-RD-09 supplies no standalone correction. The refund is therefore 6.80, which is less than the 7.50 contested and less than the whole fare, so the ruling is partial. THE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The driver's statement, 'the meter adds the extra distance', identifies no traffic cause and no rider instruction; it describes how the fare was computed rather than excusing the route. No traffic advisory covering this trip is on file: EV-ADVIS-02813-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 / POL-RD-13 — I name that artifact, its weight and its issue code as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. Because the driver named no advisory evidence id, this is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited missing artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02813) holds zero messages, so POL-RD-04's rider-requested-detour exoneration cannot be attempted (no waypoint_hint, no instruction) and no excess is excluded. No endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at null, amended_optimal_distance_km null), so POL-RD-05 cannot be run and the 9.2 km booked optimal stands. The vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 supplies no different baseline. No driver compensation arises: the rider was not billed for less distance than the trace records (no shortfall exceeding 1.0 km), and POL-RD-11 states the driver's unrecovered cost on an unjustified detour is not recoverable from the rider. ESCALATION AND REFERRALS. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers match, the trace is unimpaired and not corroboration-dependent under POL-RD-07, the timestamps agree, no exculpatory clause was invoked against a cited missing artifact, the refund is far below SGD 150.00, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. No clause produces a referral: the deviation is not material, so POL-RD-06(c) does not fire, and POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to refer (no gantry or surcharge line). The one discarded claim below was discarded by the code referee and plays no part. EXECUTION AND CONFIDENCE. The monetary effect, 6.80, does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes on issue, subject to appeal. The deciding fact — the amount charged over the quote — is carried by EV-FARE-02813 at weight 1.0, and the establishment facts by EV-GPS-02813 and EV-TRIP-02813, both at 1.0; the MISSING advisory carries no fact. The confidence cap is therefore 1.0 and my confidence is 0.95."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The absent advisory is not an escalation trigger here. No party has cited a traffic advisory as an exculpatory artifact, and POL-RD-13(1) provides that an assertion naming no evidence id cannot be invoked against an artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. Nor is any other POL-RD-10 trigger: the trip identifiers match, the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree, and the refund of 6.80 is far below SGD 150.00. The case is decidable on the record and the disputed amount should be refunded rather than held.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02813-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

